(vector (map (:adr/test-status-7010 "34 tests / 134 assertions, lint clean, demo verified end-to-end (one clean single-actuation lifecycle plus four HARD-hold cases); kotoba-lang/industry's own full test suite re-run with the local-root technology override before committing -- 7 tests / 114 assertions, all green, no pre-existing fixture referenced ISIC \"7010\""), (:adr/distinctive-check-7010 "transfer-price-outside-arms-length-range? is the FIRST instance of a GENUINELY NEW range-bound (two-sided) check shape in this fleet (grep-verified absent -- zero hits for 'transfer-pric'/'arms-length'/'arm's-length' across every prior sibling), distinct from both the existing single-bound MAXIMUM-ceiling family (9 prior instances) and MINIMUM-threshold family (8 prior instances). Grounded in OECD Transfer Pricing Guidelines' arm's-length principle, US IRC §482, Japan's 租税特別措置法第66条の4, and Germany's AStG §1"), (:adr/related (vector "2607071250-cloud-itonami-brokerage-6612-coverage" "2607071320-cloud-itonami-credit-6492-coverage" "2607071351-cloud-itonami-accounting-6920-coverage" "2607071618-cloud-itonami-marketadmin-6611-coverage" "2607071640-cloud-itonami-testlab-7120-coverage" "2607071654-cloud-itonami-clinic-8620-coverage" "2607071717-cloud-itonami-registrar-8530-coverage" "2607071732-cloud-itonami-wagering-9200-coverage" "2607071752-cloud-itonami-veterinary-7500-coverage" "2607071819-cloud-itonami-funeral-9603-coverage" "2607071849-cloud-itonami-repairshop-9521-coverage" "2607071922-cloud-itonami-parksafety-9321-coverage" "2607072715-cloud-itonami-eldercare-8730-coverage" "2607072730-cloud-itonami-museum-9102-coverage" "2607072745-cloud-itonami-conservation-9103-coverage" "2607072800-cloud-itonami-salon-9602-coverage" "2607072815-cloud-itonami-entertainment-9000-coverage" "2607072830-cloud-itonami-casework-8890-coverage" "2607072845-cloud-itonami-hospital-8610-coverage" "2607072900-cloud-itonami-facility-9311-coverage" "2607072915-cloud-itonami-school-8510-coverage" "2607080100-cloud-itonami-association-9412-coverage" "2607080200-cloud-itonami-leasing-6491-coverage" "2607080300-cloud-itonami-behavioral-8720-coverage" "2607080400-cloud-itonami-secondary-8521-coverage" "2607080500-cloud-itonami-card-6619-coverage" "2607080600-cloud-itonami-water-3600-coverage" "2607080700-cloud-itonami-telecom-6190-coverage" "2607080800-cloud-itonami-aerospace-3030-coverage" "2607080900-cloud-itonami-recovery-3830-coverage" "2607081000-cloud-itonami-consulting-7020-coverage" "2607081100-cloud-itonami-union-9420-coverage" "2607081200-cloud-itonami-congregation-9491-coverage" "2607081300-cloud-itonami-fab-2610-coverage" "2607081400-cloud-itonami-energy-3512-coverage" "2607081500-cloud-itonami-care-8810-coverage" "2607081600-cloud-itonami-navigator-8691-coverage" "2607081700-cloud-itonami-learning-8569-coverage" "2607081800-cloud-itonami-banking-6419-coverage" "2607081900-cloud-itonami-advertising-7310-coverage" "2607082100-cloud-itonami-polling-7320-coverage" "2607082200-cloud-itonami-research-7210-coverage" "2607082300-cloud-itonami-design-7410-coverage" "2607082600-cloud-itonami-nursing-8710-coverage" "2607082800-cloud-itonami-sports-8541-coverage" "2607082900-cloud-itonami-alliedhealth-8690-coverage" "2607083000-cloud-itonami-laundry-9601-coverage" "2607083300-cloud-itonami-holdco-6420-coverage" "2607083500-cloud-itonami-photo-7420-coverage" "2607083600-cloud-itonami-personalservice-9609-coverage" "2607083800-cloud-itonami-edsupport-8550-coverage" "2607032000-cloud-itonami-insurance-real-estate-coverage" "cloud-itonami-isic-6511/6512/6621/6622/6629/6520/6530/6820/6612/6492/6920/6611/7120/8620/8530/9200/7500/9603/9521/9321/8730/9102/9103/9602/9000/8890/8610/9311/8510/9412/6491/8720/8521/6619/3600/6190/3030/3830/7020/9420/9491/2610/3512/8810/8691/8569/6419/7310/7320/7210/7410/8710/8541/8690/9601/6420/7420/9609/8550 ADR-0001s" "langgraph ADR-0001")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:adr/id "2607084000"), (:adr/no-dedicated-screening-op-7010 "unlike most single-screening-op siblings, this build has NO dedicated screening op at all -- both distinctive checks are pure ground-truth numeric recomputes against the unit's own permanent fields, scoped directly to the actuation, matching advertising/7310's and navigator/8691's precedent that such checks need no separate screening op"), (:adr/fleet-maturity-before "{:implemented 65, :blueprint 19, :spec 546, :total 643}"), (:adr/next-vertical-selection-unconstrained true), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/honest-reuse-check-7010 "budget-allocation-exceeds-authorized-limit? is an honest TENTH instance of the MAXIMUM-ceiling check family (facility/school/card/recovery/care/navigator/advertising/nursing/holdco established the first nine), applying the same ceiling-only comparison to a unit's own proposed allocation against its own authorized limit, closely analogous to advertising.registry/media-spend-exceeds-authorized-budget?'s own shape -- NOT claimed as new"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607084000: `cloud-itonami-isic-7010` (activities of head offices) deepened to `:implemented`\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted.\n\n## Related\n\n- ADR-2607032000 (original insurance/real-estate batch)\n- ADR-2607083600 (`cloud-itonami-isic-9609`, other personal service activities n.e.c.)\n- ADR-2607083800 (`cloud-itonami-isic-8550`, educational support activities)\n- `cloud-itonami-isic-7010/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md` (child-repo architecture ADR)\n- `langgraph` ADR-0001 (StateGraph actor pattern)\n\n## Context\n\n`cloud-itonami-isic-7010` publishes an OSS business blueprint for\nactivities of head offices: overseeing and administering other units\nof the same enterprise or group (strategic planning, budgeting,\ngroup-wide policy). Like every prior vertical in this fleet, the\nblueprint text alone is not an implementation — this ADR records the\ngoverned-actor build that promotes `cloud-itonami-isic-7010` from\n`:blueprint` to `:implemented` in the `kotoba-lang/industry`\nregistry, the fifty-second vertical built outside ADR-2607032000's\noriginal insurance/real-estate batch.\n\n## Problem\n\n1. `cloud-itonami-isic-7010`'s blueprint described a real-world head-\n   office operating model (unit intake, group-report verification,\n   group budget/policy allocation finalization) but had no governed-\n   actor implementation: no Store, no Governor, no rollout phasing,\n   no tests.\n2. The blueprint's own text names only ONE real-world act\n   (\"finalizing a group budget/policy allocation\") — this build\n   needed the single-actuation shape.\n3. Head-office/group-oversight activities carry a genuine, real-world\n   compliance concern distinct from every prior sibling: inter-unit\n   transfer pricing must fall WITHIN an arm's-length range (both an\n   upper AND lower bound), not merely under a single ceiling like\n   this fleet's existing MAXIMUM-ceiling check family, nor merely\n   above a single floor like its MINIMUM-threshold family.\n4. This fleet already has a \"spend/allocation exceeds authorized\n   ceiling\" concept (`advertising`/7310's `media-spend-exceeds-\n   authorized-budget?`, itself the 7th MAXIMUM-ceiling instance) —\n   this build's own budget-allocation check needed to honestly\n   characterize its own reuse rather than overclaim novelty.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Single-actuation shape.** Matching `leasing`/`underwriting`/\n   `testlab`/`clinic`/`veterinary`/`funeral`/`parksafety`/`salon`/\n   `entertainment`/`facility`/`consulting`/`advertising`/`polling`/\n   `research`/`design`/`sports`/`alliedhealth`/`photo`/\n   `personalservice`/`edsupport`'s single-actuation shape, `high-\n   stakes` is the one-member set `#{:actuation/finalize-allocation}`.\n2. **Entity and op shape.** Primary entity `unit` (subsidiary/\n   business unit). Three ops: `:unit/intake`, `:report/verify`,\n   `:actuation/finalize-allocation` (high-stakes). No dedicated\n   screening op — both distinctive checks are ground-truth numeric\n   recomputes scoped directly to the actuation, matching\n   `advertising`/7310's and `navigator`/8691's precedent.\n3. **`transfer-price-outside-arms-length-range?` — the first\n   instance of a new range-bound check shape.** Grep-verified absent\n   (zero hits for \"transfer-pric\"/\"arms-length\"/\"arm's-length\" across\n   every prior sibling). Recomputes `(or (< price range-min) (> price\n   range-max))` directly from the unit's own recorded fields — a\n   two-sided check, distinct from this fleet's existing single-bound\n   families. Grounded in OECD Transfer Pricing Guidelines' arm's-\n   length principle, US IRC §482, Japan's 租税特別措置法第66条の4, and\n   Germany's AStG §1. Gates only `:actuation/finalize-allocation`.\n4. **`budget-allocation-exceeds-authorized-limit?` — an honest tenth\n   MAXIMUM-ceiling instance, not claimed as new.** `facility`/\n   `school`/`card`/`recovery`/`care`/`navigator`/`advertising`/\n   `nursing`/`holdco` established the first nine instances; this\n   build's reuse is the tenth, closely analogous to `advertising.\n   registry/media-spend-exceeds-authorized-budget?`'s own shape.\n   Gates only `:actuation/finalize-allocation`.\n5. **Dedicated double-actuation-guard boolean.** `:allocation-\n   finalized?` on the `unit` record, never a single `:status` value.\n6. **Store protocol, MemStore + DatomicStore parity**, proven via\n   `test/headoffice/store_contract_test.clj`. The per-entity accessor\n   is safely named `unit` directly.\n7. **Phase 0→3 rollout** — Phase 3's `:auto` set is `{:unit/intake}`\n   only; the actuation is permanently excluded from every phase's\n   `:auto` set.\n8. **No bespoke domain capability lib** — this blueprint's own\n   `:itonami.blueprint/required-technologies` names no domain-\n   specific capability beyond the generic stack.\n9. **Mock + LLM advisor pair** — `mock-advisor` default everywhere,\n   `llm-advisor` with a defensive EDN-proposal parser.\n10. **No `blueprint.edn` field-sync fixes needed** — the `isic-`\n    prefixed `:id` and `:required-technologies`/`:optional-\n    technologies` already matched the `kotoba-lang/industry` registry\n    exactly; only the `:maturity` field itself needed adding.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Sixty-sixth actor in this fleet (65 implemented before this\n  build).\n- Introduces a genuinely NEW range-bound check shape (first instance,\n  grep-verified absent from every prior sibling), distinct from both\n  existing single-bound check families in this fleet.\n- Documents an honest TENTH instance of the MAXIMUM-ceiling check\n  family, not claimed as new.\n- `MemStore` ‖ `DatomicStore` parity is proven by `test/headoffice/\n  store_contract_test.clj`.\n- Fleet maturity: `:implemented` 65 → 66, `:blueprint` 19 → 18,\n  `:spec` 546 unchanged, total 643.\n- Test status: 34 tests / 134 assertions, lint clean, demo verified\n  end-to-end.\n- `kotoba-lang/industry`'s full test suite re-run with the local-root\n  `technology` override before committing — 7 tests / 114 assertions,\n  all green, no pre-existing fixture referenced ISIC \"7010\".\n- This build's `deps.edn` used the CURRENT `kotoba-lang/langgraph`/\n  `langchain` coordinates from the start (see `holdco`/6420's own\n  ADR-0001 for the upstream-rename context this build inherited).\n- Next vertical selection remains unconstrained under the standing\n  authorization.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|---|---|\n| Framing `transfer-price-outside-arms-length-range?` as a MAXIMUM-ceiling reuse (upper bound only) | Real transfer-pricing law requires a price to fall WITHIN a range on both sides, not merely under a ceiling — a single-bound characterization would misrepresent the real-world compliance requirement |\n| A dedicated screening op for either distinctive check | Both checks are pure ground-truth recomputes needing no proposal inspection, matching `advertising`/7310's and `navigator`/8691's precedent that such checks are scoped directly to the actuation |\n| A dual-actuation shape (budget + policy as two acts) | The blueprint's own text consistently names only ONE real-world act |\n\n## References\n\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-7010/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md`\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-7010/README.edn`\n- `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-7010/docs/business-model.md`\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/industry/resources/kotoba/industry/registry.edn` (entry `\"7010\"`)"), (:adr/pattern-7010 "sealed HeadOffice-LLM + independent Group Oversight Governor + append-only audit ledger, modeled closely on all sixty-five prior actors; FIFTY-SECOND build outside ADR-2607032000's original insurance/real-estate batch (after 6612, 6492, 6920, 6611, 7120, 8620, 8530, 9200, 7500, 9603, 9521, 9321, 8730, 9102, 9103, 9602, 9000, 8890, 8610, 9311, 8510, 9412, 6491, 8720, 8521, 6619, 3600, 6190, 3030, 3830, 7020, 9420, 9491, 2610, 3512, 8810, 8691, 8569, 6419, 7310, 7320, 7210, 7410, 8710, 8541, 8690, 9601, 6420, 7420, 9609, 8550)"), (:adr/fleet-maturity-after "{:implemented 66, :blueprint 18, :spec 546, :total 643}"), (:adr/no-bespoke-capability-lib-7010 "this blueprint's own :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies names no domain-specific capability beyond the generic robotics/identity/forms/dmn/bpmn/audit-ledger stack -- there was no capability-lib decision to make at all"), (:adr/single-actuation-7010 "this blueprint's own README/business-model.md/operator-guide.md text consistently names only ONE real-world act (finalizing a group budget/policy allocation), so this build uses the single-actuation shape (#{:actuation/finalize-allocation}), matching leasing/underwriting/testlab/clinic/veterinary/funeral/parksafety/salon/entertainment/facility/consulting/advertising/polling/research/design/sports/alliedhealth/photo/personalservice/edsupport's precedent"), (:adr/blueprint-already-correct-7010 "this repo's blueprint.edn already had the correct isic- prefixed :id and correctly populated :required-technologies/:optional-technologies matching the kotoba-lang/industry registry's own entry for \"7010\" exactly -- only the :maturity field itself needed adding"), (:adr/date "2026-07-08"), (:adr/scope-note "this is a NEW ADR because ISIC 7010 (activities of head offices) contributes a genuinely new range-bound check shape (transfer-price-outside-arms-length-range?), distinct from both existing single-bound check families, warranting its own record per this fleet's standing per-vertical-ADR convention"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/deps-edn-current-coordinates-from-start-7010 "this build's deps.edn used the CURRENT io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph + langchain coordinates and :local/root paths from the very start, inheriting the fix holdco/6420's build discovered and documented -- see holdco/6420's own ADR-0001 for the full upstream-rename context (a repo transfer + rename, internal namespaces unchanged)"), (:adr/deepened-to-implemented "cloud-itonami-isic-7010"), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isic-7010 (activities of head offices) deepened to :implemented -- fifty-second vertical outside the original batch"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))